th the information at hand, I have to pass and wait for the Landlord to play.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The teammate (Left) has played a pair of Jacks (JJ) to beat the Landlord\'s pair of 5s. As the current player sitting between the teammate and the Landlord (Right), my goal is to assist the teammate. The Landlord has only 5 cards left, making this a critical phase. Playing my Pair of Aces (AA) would beat my teammate\'s hand, effectively blocking the teammate and potentially saving the Landlord from having to play a high pair (like QQ or KK) to stay in the game. It is strategically better to Pass and force the Landlord to beat the Jacks. If the Landlord plays a higher pair, I can choose to use my Aces or 2s on the next turn, or let my teammate handle it. If the Landlord passes, my teammate keeps control.\n\nReason: Teammate played a strong blocking pair (JJ). Beating it with AA wastes a top pair and disrupts the teammate\'s control. Passing forces the Landlord to spend high cards (QQ, KK, AA, 22) or lose the turn. I should save my AA and 22 to catch the Landlord if he beats the Jacks.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
